# Hybrid Analytics Implementation Plan

---

## Layer 0 — Script Preloading Strategy

This is the **performance foundation** that must be correct before any SDK loads.

### Current State
[layout.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/app/layout.tsx) already has `<link rel="preconnect">` and `<link rel="dns-prefetch">` for `connect.facebook.net` and `www.googletagmanager.com`. But:
- No preloading for Microsoft Clarity domains
- All scripts are injected via raw DOM manipulation (`document.createElement("script")`) — this bypasses Next.js's resource scheduler
- No use of `next/script` component at all — meaning no browser priority hints

### What We'll Do

#### [MODIFY] [layout.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/app/layout.tsx)

**Preconnect hints** (add these to `<head>`):
```html
<!-- Microsoft Clarity -->
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.clarity.ms" crossOrigin="anonymous" />
<link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.clarity.ms" />

<!-- Clarity script origin -->
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://z.clarity.ms" crossOrigin="anonymous" />
<link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://z.clarity.ms" />
```

**GTM script loading via `next/script`** (replaces DOM injection in [initGTM](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts#11-45)):
```tsx
// Rendered conditionally when GTM ID is available from config
<Script
  id="gtm-loader"
  src={`https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id=${gtmId}`}
  strategy="afterInteractive"  // Loads after page is interactive — does not block LCP/FID
/>
```

> **Why `afterInteractive` not `lazyOnload`?**  
> `lazyOnload` delays until all resources are idle, which can mean GTM misses early events (e.g., `page_view` fired before GTM loads). `afterInteractive` is the sweet spot — doesn't block render, but fires before the user has a chance to interact.

**Clarity script via `next/script`**:
```tsx
<Script
  id="clarity-loader"
  src="https://www.clarity.ms/tag/YOUR_PROJECT_ID"
  strategy="afterInteractive"
/>
```

**Facebook fbevents.js** — stays as inline snippet (GTM will handle it via a GTM tag, not loaded by `next/script`). FB Pixel is best loaded *through GTM* so GTM can control consent.

#### [MODIFY] [AnalyticsProvider.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/AnalyticsProvider.tsx)
- Remove the [initGTM()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts#11-45) DOM script injection (GTM script is now loaded by `next/script` in layout)
- Remove the [initGA()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/google-analytics.ts#30-63) DOM script injection (GA4 is now a GTM tag, not directly loaded)
- Remove the [initPixel()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#85-155) call (FB Pixel is now a GTM tag)
- Keep only: `initClarity()` stub for identify/tag, and the `dataLayer` pre-initialization

#### [MODIFY] [gtm.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts)
- Remove the `document.createElement("script")` injection from [initGTM()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts#11-45)
- [initGTM()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts#11-45) now only sets up the `dataLayer` array and pushes the `gtm.start` event
- The actual script tag is in layout.tsx, so it loads with proper browser-level `<link rel="preload">` hinting

