## Background

The codebase already has a **partially-built** client-side analytics layer:
- ✅ [AnalyticsProvider.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/AnalyticsProvider.tsx) — config from API, stale-while-revalidate cache, idle-deferred SDK init
- ✅ [facebook-pixel.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts) — FB Pixel client events (ViewContent, AddToCart, etc.)
- ✅ [google-analytics.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/google-analytics.ts) — GA4 via gtag.js
- ✅ [gtm.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts) — GTM bootstrap & [pushDataLayer()](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/gtm.ts#48-57) helper
- ✅ [useAnalytics.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/useAnalytics.ts) — unified hook

**What is missing (the full gap list):**

| Gap | Severity |
|-----|----------|
| Microsoft Clarity — not touched anywhere | High |
| GTM data layer pushes are **commented out** everywhere to avoid double-counting | High |
| No **deduplication `event_id`** sent alongside client events | High |
| No server-side **Facebook CAPI** (no backend route, no hashing) | Critical |
| No **cookie handoff** (`fbp`, `fbc`, `_ga` → API payload) | Critical |
| `system_config` / [types.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/types.ts) don't include Clarity or CAPI config keys | Medium |
| [AnalyticsProvider](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/AnalyticsProvider.tsx#98-226) does not forward user identity to FB Advanced Matching | Medium |

---

## Architecture Decision

```
Browser                                GTM Container
─────────                              ─────────────
dataLayer.push(event)  ────────────►  triggers FB Pixel tag
                                       triggers GA4 tag
                                       triggers Clarity tag (via Custom HTML)

                        (Purchase only)
Express.js API ────────────────────────► Facebook CAPI (server-to-server)
                                         ↳ hashed PII (SHA-256)
                                         ↳ same event_id as browser
                                         ↳ Facebook deduplicates both hits
```

**Core principle:** GTM becomes the **single source of truth** for client events. We **remove** the direct FB Pixel / gtag.js calls from [useAnalytics](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/useAnalytics.ts#46-125) and replace them with clean `dataLayer.push()` calls. GTM then fires all tags. This fixes the double-counting issue and is the industry standard.

**Microsoft Clarity** is CSP-safe and injected during GTM init (one `<script>` tag).

**Facebook CAPI** fires **only** from the Express API for high-value conversion events (Purchase, CompleteRegistration). The browser still fires the same event client-side via GTM. Both carry the same `event_id` so Meta deduplicates.

