### Layer 1.5 — Data Layer Architecture

The **data layer** is a JavaScript array (`window.dataLayer`) that acts as the communication bus between your site and GTM. It must be initialized **before GTM loads** — otherwise early events (like `page_view`) get dropped.

#### Initialization Order (Critical)

```html
<!-- Step 1: dataLayer init — must run BEFORE gtm.js loads -->
<script>
  window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  // Pre-load page context so it's available to all subsequent GTM events
  window.dataLayer.push({
    pageType: 'unknown',       // overridden per-page by route-level pushes
    user_logged_in: false,     // overridden by AnalyticsProvider when auth is known
    currency: 'BDT',
  });
</script>

<!-- Step 2: GTM script (via next/script afterInteractive) -->
<script src="https://www.googletagmanager.com/gtm.js?id=GTM-XXXX" async></script>
```

#### Data Layer Schema (Typed)

All `dataLayer.push()` calls will follow a strict schema. A new `DataLayerEvent` type will be added to [types.ts](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/types.ts):

```typescript
// E-commerce events follow GA4 ecommerce schema
type EcommerceItem = {
  item_id: string;       // Product SKU ID
  item_name: string;     // Product name
  item_category?: string;
  price?: number;
  quantity?: number;
};

type DataLayerEvent = {
  event: string;               // GTM trigger name, e.g. 'purchase', 'add_to_cart'
  event_id?: string;           // UUID for deduplication
  ecommerce?: {
    currency: string;
    value: number;
    transaction_id?: string;   // order ID — for purchase event
    items: EcommerceItem[];
  };
  user_data?: {
    em?: string;               // hashed email (SHA-256) for FB Advanced Matching
    ph?: string;               // hashed phone
    external_id?: string;      // user ID
  };
  // Custom dimensions
  user_logged_in?: boolean;
  page_type?: string;          // 'product', 'category', 'checkout', 'home'
};
```

#### The Ecommerce Clear Pattern (GA4 Standard)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Before every ecommerce event push, you **must** push `{ ecommerce: null }` first. Without this, GTM may carry over product data from a previous event, corrupting your analytics.

```typescript
// In pushEcommerceEvent() in gtm.ts:
export function pushEcommerceEvent(eventName: string, data: DataLayerEvent) {
  window.dataLayer.push({ ecommerce: null }); // ← Clear previous ecommerce data
  window.dataLayer.push({ event: eventName, ...data });
}
```

#### Pre-Initialization in [layout.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/app/layout.tsx)

A new inline `<Script id="datalayer-init" strategy="beforeInteractive">` block in [layout.tsx](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/app/layout.tsx) will:
1. Initialize `window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || []`
2. Push initial page context (currency, environment)
3. This runs **synchronously before hydration** — so no event is ever dropped

```tsx
<Script id="datalayer-init" strategy="beforeInteractive">
  {`window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
  window.dataLayer.push({ currency: 'BDT', environment: '${process.env.NODE_ENV}' });`}
</Script>
```

