## Event Flow Summary

### Purchase Event (Hybrid)

```
1. User clicks "Place Order"
2. Frontend generates event_id = crypto.randomUUID()
3. Frontend reads fbp + fbc cookies
4. API call: POST /order with { ..., fbp, fbc, capi_event_id: event_id }
5. API saves order → returns { orderId }
   └─ API async: sendCapiEvent("Purchase", { event_id, fbp, fbc, value, ... })
6. Frontend: dataLayer.push({ event: "purchase", event_id, ecommerce: {...} })
   └─ GTM fires FB Pixel tag: fbq("track","Purchase",{...}, {eventID: event_id})
   └─ GTM fires GA4 tag: purchase event
7. Meta receives BOTH hits with same event_id → keeps best one → no duplicate
```

### All Other Events (Client-Only via GTM)
```
ViewContent / AddToCart / InitiateCheckout / Search / PageView
└─ dataLayer.push({ event: "...", ecommerce: {...} })
   └─ GTM fires all configured tags
```

