## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification Steps

1. **GTM Data Layer** — Open browser DevTools console on the shop and run:
   ```js
   window.dataLayer // Should show all pushed events
   ```
   Use the [GTM Preview mode](https://tagmanager.google.com) to see tags firing in real-time.

2. **Facebook Pixel Helper** — Install the [Facebook Pixel Helper](https://chrome.google.com/webstore/detail/facebook-pixel-helper/) Chrome extension. Visit the shop homepage. Add a product to cart. Proceed to checkout. Confirm events: [PageView](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#168-172), [ViewContent](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#173-184), [AddToCart](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#185-196), [InitiateCheckout](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#197-207) fire correctly with correct values.

3. **Microsoft Clarity** — After adding your Clarity Project ID, visit the Clarity dashboard. Check that session recordings appear within 1-2 minutes of page visits at [clarity.microsoft.com](https://clarity.microsoft.com).

4. **Facebook CAPI (Server-Side)** — In Meta Events Manager → Test Events panel, set a `TEST_EVENT_CODE`. Place a test order with a real payment. Verify the [Purchase](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_shop/lib/analytics/facebook-pixel.ts#208-219) event appears **twice** (once from browser Pixel, once from CAPI) but Meta shows a **deduplicated count of 1**.

5. **No Double-Counting in GA4** — In GA4 Realtime report, add a product to cart. Confirm only **one** `add_to_cart` event fires (not two).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You will need to configure GTM **tags, triggers, and variables** in the GTM web interface for the events to fire. The code only pushes to `dataLayer` — GTM reads it and fires based on your tag configuration. I will include a GTM setup guide in the walkthrough after implementation.

> [!WARNING]  
> The `META_CAPI_ACCESS_TOKEN` must **never** be stored in the frontend. It lives only in `system_config` (database) and is read server-side. Never commit it to [.env](file:///d:/gcp/gcp_graduatefashion_api/.env).
